0..76 Comment "// Temporary access. `var c = e;` keeps a value for the rest of a block, and"
77..157 Comment "// `access c as v { … }` lends it to the view `v`, which the body ends exactly"
158..237 Comment "// once: `resume(v, e)` writes `e` back, `abort(v)` leaves the held value as it"
238..317 Comment "// was and runs the access\'s `unwind` clause instead. The unwind runs under the"
318..390 Comment "// empty row, and an access with none unwinds by doing nothing. The loan"
391..468 Comment "// follows Rust\'s mutable borrow, ended once (_The Rust Reference_, § Borrow"
469..483 Comment "// operators)."
